node -e "
const fs=require('fs');const f='Design/GDD.md';let t=fs.readFileSync(f,'utf8');
const r=(a,b)=>{if(!t.includes(a))throw new Error(a.slice(0,60));t=t.split(a).join(b);};
r('Status: **v0.38, 2026-11-13**','Status: **v0.39, 2026-11-13**');
r('- v0.38 (2026-11-13): owner, after seeing it in the arena','- v0.39 (2026-11-13): owner, after playing the package: **the skill trees are two pages** (tabs; Q / E, L1 / L2 / R1), and each page takes its tree\'s whole look (spells = RPG, weapons = cyberpunk); the other menus both eras share take **the current era\'s look** (past = RPG, future = cyberpunk) instead of the held item\'s; I opens the inventory; the spell page gets a calmer, darker background. **The weapon tree becomes a hub with three gun branches, Cyberpunk style:** Heavy Rounds on top, then Pistol, Rifle and Shotgun; choosing one opens that gun\'s page, with a Back button. Architect, provisional: the nine existing perks are regrouped by theme with their effects unchanged (§18 \"Weapon tree\").\n- v0.38 (2026-11-13): owner, after seeing it in the arena');
r('  - **Skill trees** keep the split whatever the held item: the spell tree is a stone tablet','  - **Skill trees** (v0.39): two pages behind tabs, and each page takes its tree\'s look for the whole screen, whatever the era or the held item. The other menus both eras share (inventory, pause, death) take the current era\'s look. The spell tree is a tablet');
r('- **Weapon tree (owner, v0.24):** Heavy Rounds','- **Weapon tree, v0.39 (owner: a hub with gun branches, \"similar to Cyberpunk\"):** Heavy Rounds stays the first perk, on the hub page. Under it, three gun emblems: **Pistol**, **Rifle**, **Shotgun**. Choosing one (Enter or a click) opens that gun\'s page; a Back button (and Esc / B) returns to the hub. **Provisional (architect):** the nine perks below keep their effects, costs and ranks exactly (so §19\'s balance and the 36-point budget are unchanged) and are regrouped by theme: **Pistol** (precision) = Deadeye, Marksman -> Precision Recovery; **Rifle** (sustained fire) = Long Shot, Quick Trigger -> Steady Grip; **Shotgun** (close range) = Point Blank -> Arcane Conduit, Rapid Reload. The first perks of every branch need only Heavy Rounds. Two prerequisites changed so each branch stands alone: Rapid Reload now needs Heavy Rounds (was Quick Trigger) and Arcane Conduit needs Point Blank (was Marksman). The perks that work on every gun say \"All guns\" in their description. Gun-specific versions of the shared perks are a possible next step if the owner wants each branch to touch only its gun.\n- **Weapon tree (owner, v0.24, superseded by v0.39 above):** Heavy Rounds');
fs.writeFileSync(f,t);console.log('ok')"

